# Google Maps API Configuration
#
# To use this app, you need a Google Maps API key.
# Follow these steps:
#
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Create a new project or select an existing one
# 3. Enable these APIs:
#    - Maps JavaScript API
#    - Places API
# 4. Create credentials (API Key)
# 5. Copy your API key and paste it in index.html
#
# Find this line in index.html (near the bottom):
# <script src="https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/js?key=YOUR_API_KEY&libraries=places&callback=initMap" async defer></script>
#
# Replace YOUR_API_KEY with your actual key:
# <script src="https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/js?key=AIzaSyXXXXXXXXXX&libraries=places&callback=initMap" async defer></script>

GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=YOUR_API_KEY_HERE

# Optional: Restrict your API key to specific domains for security
# In Google Cloud Console, under API Key restrictions, add:
# - http://localhost:8000/*
# - https://yourdomain.com/*
